y in staging and also unhealthy). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator partial failure, leaving the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt to v2.3.0 completed in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west, and eu-west; healthy; error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate v2.3.1 failure cause, and investigate the orchestrator partial failure during the first rollback attempt."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so I'll check whether it was created before retrying. A retry could page the on-call engineer twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015HpNMTERhqoF7BXegVM1BC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It reports healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed. I retried once and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to open the SEV2 incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying, and the incident was already created as **INC-0001** with the summary of actions above. I did not create a duplicate.\n\nFollow-up for the team: find the cause of the v2.3.1 health-check failures, and look into the orchestrator partial failure during the first rollback attempt.", "type": "text"}]}]}